  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Night Planner",
    "overview": "Form looks like a calm dark desk at the end of the day. One plan is set down quietly, and colour appears only where the plan lives: the dial's arc, the plan's title on Today, and one glyph per row in a list. Everything else is moonlight text on a deep navy night. The system is calm, precise and honest. It shows a likely range instead of a falsely exact number, says which inputs it used, and names the reasons.\n\nDensity is low and the rhythm is generous: one focal element per screen, grouped by space before lines, and lines before containers. There are no cards. Depth comes from one raised surface (the bottom sheet) and nothing else. Type does the work of hierarchy: Manrope, set tight, for what you decide on; Source Sans 3 for everything you read.\n\nDark is the app theme (user decision, 1 Oct 2026). The light theme (\"Dawn\" and \"Ink\") stays defined and is used in the gallery.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "One flat dark canvas; colour reserved for the plan.",
      "One focal element per screen: the dial on Today, the plan glyphs on Week, the fit sentence on Progress.",
      "Honest numbers: a range, an inputs count, signed drivers.",
      "Tight display type, open body type, 48 pt targets everywhere."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Plan Owns Colour Rule",
        "body": "A plan hue appears only where that plan is shown: the dial arc and range bracket, the plan title on Today, and the plan glyph in a list row. In lists the plan's word is plain moonlight text.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Never Alone Rule",
        "body": "A plan is never colour alone. Every plan shows its glyph (Dumbbell, Footprints, Moon, Focus) and its label.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Night Field Rule",
        "body": "In dark, Today has no colour field. The field token equals Night, because the dial's reveal cover is drawn in the field colour and must match what is behind it.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
